triage |bug_id, previous_status, proposed_status, implementation_complete, source_evidence, test_evidence, scope_limit, next_step|
    cargo_test_lib_129_failures_triage_2026-08-10, open, fixing, false, "Aggregate 129-failure premise is outdated; the November5 retained full-lib measurement reports 4561 passed/27 failed/6 ignored, then one Vulkan registry-pin fix leaves26 recorded residuals. Current pipeline/native_project/tests.rs has poison-recovering environment locks, a partial category repair, not proof all remaining compiler/runtime/import tests are fixed.", "doc/08_tracking/bug/cargo_test_lib_129_failures_triage_2026-08-10.md November5 report names remaining native_project, pipeline, Vulkan, typed-dict, MIR, import-loader/cache/font/resolver groups. No new full lib run was executed in this lane.", "Current failure count at87 is UNKNOWN; neither old129 nor retained26 is asserted as the current count. Source inspection cannot establish complete closure of this heterogeneous suite.", "After first admitted runtime/bootstrap scheduling permits, execute one finite isolated Rust-owner lib suite, retain exact failed test identities and environment, then repair remaining independent owners; preserve partial fixes."
    jit_text_repeat_dispatch_and_silent_error_substitution_2026-08-01, open, fixing, false, "codegen/instr/calls.rs and closures_structs.rs route repeat to rt_string_repeat and parse_int/parse_i32/parse_i64 to Option-preserving rt_string_parse_int; the codegen sffi_alias_target unit assertion pins parse_i64. The original document's latest November5 E2 correction retracts its float-Option complaint. Residual ptr ownership is unresolved: interpreter_method/string.rs clones into PINNED_STRINGS, while neither reviewed compiled method dispatch table contains a ptr route.", "Existing parse_i64 alias assertion is meaningful for its resolved subcase; no real compiled/interpreter ptr-lifetime parity regression was identified. The document records repeat/fallback and49 methods already repaired; those partial results do not settle ptr.", "Whole record remains the ptr-lifetime owner decision, not another repeat transcription or fabricated raw-float defect. No JIT/runtime tests rerun.", "Define and review the ptr SFFI ownership/lifetime contract across engines, implement a matching compiled route or explicit refusal as accepted, then execute lifetime/owner and parity regressions."
    native_interp_logical_and_or_llc_type_mismatch_2026-07-16, open, fix-implemented-verification-pending, true, "src/compiler/70.backend/backend/_MirToLlvm/core_codegen.spl:2259 translate_const now derives previously undeclared SSA constant destination types from the instruction MirType while retaining registered locals; it records the matching local/value type before emitting a pointer/string Store. This directly removes the original renamed-string-constant i64 versus ptr mismatch. Fix code/comment and regression were present through ancestor9e7e7a526edb and remain in87.", "scripts/check/check-native-seed-parity.shs:1289 write_case_interp_logical_bool builds the exact t() and t() interpolation repro; line2281 passes it to run_strict_dual_backend_case with exact expected output v=true. These are meaningful compile/run controls, not a source-text tautology. Focused llvm_copy_move_alloc_spec.spl:362-372 also asserts pointer Store/no double inttoptr, but its build_cross_block_string_const_module helper has no definition under src/test at87 and its raw-GEP expectation predates boxed-text lowering; it is NOT counted as executable PASS.", "Original constant-type implementation is source-fixed. No pure-Simple self-hosted run or native dual-backend PASS is claimed; the broken focused helper is a verification gap to repair, not evidence of success. No broad compiler/MCP qualification.", "Repair the focused regression helper/oracle against current boxed-text emission, then run the valid exact interpolation strict dual-backend case using the admitted rebuilt producer and retain real object/executable/output evidence."
    strict-field-forwarding-opt-in-20261027, open, fixing, false, "src/compiler/20.hir/hir_lowering/_Expressions/accessor_forwarding.spl:15-21 retains the workaround tag, cached SIMPLE_STRICT_FIELD_FORWARDING environment gate and default-off state; lower_accessor_read still errors only under the flag and otherwise calls warn_undefined_field. The implementation therefore has not completed the documented unconditional-strict removal plan.", "test/01_unit/compiler/hir/accessor_getter_forwarding_spec.spl has meaningful on/off warning/error, real-field and accessor cases. They pin the workaround behavior, not removal. The documented0/673 per-file census is expressly only a lower bound without imported owner tables.", "A partial/per-file census cannot prove the full compiler graph is ready for unconditional strict field checking. Current source still contains the opt-in and reset paths.", "Use the full semantic module graph to census and repair undefined reads, then remove the flag/cache/reset/env path and replace on/off tests with unconditional-error regression coverage before qualification."
    native_jit_crypto_tls13_pbkdf2_no_extern_c_implementation, open, fixing, false, "Some original missing providers are now implemented: Rust runtime/src/value/sffi/hash/sha256.rs exports extern-C rt_tls13_sha256, and runtime_native.c has the corresponding TLS hash owner. However common/src/runtime_symbols.rs still registers rt_pbkdf2_hmac_sha256 and rt_native_profile_count/event; inspected runtime-native/simple_core/Rust-runtime owners contain no corresponding PBKDF2 native export. compiler/interpreter_extern/pbkdf2.rs:60 remains the interpreter-only &[Value] handler registered through insert_simple at mod.rs:3116.", "interpreter_extern/pbkdf2.rs::tests::dispatch_sha256_c4096 checks the real PBKDF2 digest c5e478... and is meaningful interpreter evidence only. It does not exercise a native/JIT ABI provider. No native vectors/provider-link run or complete original symbol-family qualification exists in this audit.", "A newly added SHA256 provider is only a subset of the original TLS13/PBKDF2/Ed25519/SIMD/profile inventory. Missing PBKDF2 plus stale profile registrations prevent whole-scope pending/fixed classification; no cryptographic behavior is inferred from registry names.", "Inventory all original live native/JIT symbols and explicit unsupported contracts, resolve orphan profile registrations, implement missing providers through reviewed owners, then run real ABI-link and cryptographic known-answer tests for each required lane."
    type_alias_swapped_winner_is_inert_2026-08-01, open, fixing, false, "src/compiler/20.hir/hir_types.spl::define_with_binding at87 includes Class/Struct/Enum/Trait in is_type_symbol but still excludes TypeAlias, so aliases remain later-write allocations. hir_lowering/type_aliases.spl now stores type_alias_targets and lower_named_symbol_kind consults their representation; the old target-never-stored/inert premise is no longer valid. The duplicate-alias winner contract is not fixed in the authoritative87 tree.", "test/01_unit/compiler/hir/type_alias_representation_spec.spl has real parsed generic-chain, defaults, cycle and declaration-scope assertions, which prove authored transparency scenarios, not first-alias-winner retention. The private reviewed first-write candidate is not a landed source fix at87 and was not executed.", "Do not promote this record merely because alias transparency landed; transparency exposes the missing first-write policy. Nominal/value collision safety must accompany any reuse policy; no runtime PASS.", "Complete and land the reviewed first-write/retained-kind-safe implementation with duplicate divergent alias targets plus class/struct/value collision-order regressions, then execute on an admitted self-hosted compiler."
